 (state count full byTime)←StormRule(state signature now ceiling resetAfter repeatAfter);keep;ind;byCount;age;due
⍝ Applies the storm guard's rules to one crash. Changes nothing on disk.\\
⍝ `state` is what `NewStormState` and `ReadStormFile` return, `now` the time of the crash in seconds (UTC),
⍝ `ceiling`, `resetAfter` and `repeatAfter` are the parameters `stormCeiling`, `stormResetAfter` and
⍝ `stormRepeatAfter`.\\
⍝ Returns the updated `state`, the number of occurrences of `signature`, a Boolean that is 1 when the crash
⍝ gets the full treatment, and a Boolean that is 1 when it gets it because of the time limit alone.\\
⍝ The full treatment requires that the signature is due and that the ceiling allows it:
⍝ * it is due when the count is at least twice the count at which the signature last got the full treatment
⍝ * it is also due when its last full treatment is at least `repeatAfter` hours old; 0 switches this off
⍝ * the ceiling allows it when fewer than `ceiling` crashes got the full treatment within the last hour\\
⍝ A signature that has not occurred for `resetAfter` hours starts afresh.
 keep←(now-state.lasts)<resetAfter×3600
 state.(signatures counts lastFulls firsts lasts lastFullTimes)←keep∘/¨state.(signatures counts lastFulls firsts lasts lastFullTimes)
 state.fulls←((now-state.fulls)<3600)/state.fulls
 ind←state.signatures⍳⊂signature
 :If ind>≢state.signatures
     state.signatures,←⊂signature
     state.counts,←0
     state.lastFulls,←0
     state.firsts,←now
     state.lasts,←now
     state.lastFullTimes,←now
 :EndIf
 state.counts[ind]+←1
 state.lasts[ind]←now
 count←ind⊃state.counts
 byCount←count≥2×ind⊃state.lastFulls
 age←now-ind⊃state.lastFullTimes
 due←byCount∨(0<repeatAfter)∧age≥repeatAfter×3600
 full←due∧ceiling>≢state.fulls
 byTime←full∧~byCount
 :If full
     state.lastFulls[ind]←count
     state.lastFullTimes[ind]←now
     state.fulls,←now
 :EndIf
